.IX Title "LucyX::Search::ProximityQuery 3pm"
.TH LucyX::Search::ProximityQuery 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
LucyX::Search::ProximityQuery \- Query matching an ordered list of terms.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 6
\&    my $proximity_query = LucyX::Search::ProximityQuery\->new( 
\&        field  => \*(Aqcontent\*(Aq,
\&        terms  => [qw( the who )],
\&        within => 10,    # match within 10 positions
\&    );
\&    my $hits = $searcher\->hits( query => $proximity_query );
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
ProximityQuery is a subclass of Query for matching
against an ordered sequence of terms.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 5
\&    my $proximity_query = LucyX::Search::ProximityQuery\->new(
\&        field  => $field,   # required
\&        terms  => $terms,   # required
\&        within => $within,  # required
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Create a new ProximityQuery.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBfield\fR \- The field that the phrase must occur in.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBterms\fR \- The ordered array of terms that must match.
.SH METHODS
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS get_field
.IX Subsection "get_field"
.Vb 1
\&    my $string = $proximity_query\->get_field();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor for object’s field attribute.
.SS get_terms
.IX Subsection "get_terms"
.Vb 1
\&    my $arrayref = $proximity_query\->get_terms();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor for object’s array of terms.
.SS get_within
.IX Subsection "get_within"
.Vb 1
\&    my $int = $proximity_query\->get_within();
.Ve
.PP
Accessor for object’s within attribute.
.SS make_compiler
.IX Subsection "make_compiler"
.Vb 5
\&    my $compiler = $proximity_query\->make_compiler(
\&        searcher    => $searcher,     # required
\&        boost       => $boost,        # required
\&        subordinate => $subordinate,  # default: false
\&    );
.Ve
.PP
Abstract factory method returning a Compiler derived from this Query.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBsearcher\fR \- A Searcher.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBboost\fR \- A scoring multiplier.
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBsubordinate\fR \- Indicates whether the Query is a subquery (as
opposed to a top-level query).  If false, the implementation must
invoke \fBnormalize()\fR on the newly minted Compiler object before returning
it.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
LucyX::Search::ProximityQuery isa Lucy::Search::Query isa Clownfish::Obj.
